# quiet_handlers.allow — handlers that are QUIET ON PURPOSE, with the reason.
# Format: filename.py:function   # reason   # date
# An entry here silences verify_silent_degradation.py for that handler.
# Empty-reason entries are worthless — the reason IS the entry. Review >180d.
#
# The bar for adding a line: the quietness is an ENTRYPOINT-LEVEL contract
# (launchd/hook must not break) — not "this function is annoying to fix".

session_sweep.py:main          # launchd entrypoint — exit 0 contract; failure is recorded via degraded() upstream  # 2026-08-08
mission_board.py:main          # board must never break its caller; render failures leave prior HTML + stderr note  # 2026-08-08
mission_brief.py:main          # same contract as mission_board  # 2026-08-08
degrade.py:_record             # the degradation recorder must never itself raise — quietness here is the feature  # 2026-08-08
